{"id": "EUVD-2026-86024", "enisaUuid": "a4d1fc53-61ad-301a-9663-dc289cde0694", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ibm: emac: mal: fix potential system hang in mal_remove()\n\nnapi_disable() is not idempotent and calling it on an already-disabled\nor unenabled NAPI context will cause the kernel to spin indefinitely\nwaiting for the NAPI_STATE_SCHED bit to clear.\n\nIn mal_remove(), napi_disable() is called unconditionally. If no MACs were\nregistered, NAPI was never enabled. Also, if they were registered but\nsubsequently unregistered, NAPI was already disabled in\nmal_unregister_commac(). In either case, calling napi_disable() causes\nthe kernel to hang upon module removal.\n\nFix this by only calling napi_disable() in mal_remove() if the commac list\nis not empty (which implies NAPI is enabled).", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c1c814a662d9c81959eba591bb52b24639390f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34c4cae51718d6f393415e01c61314c1bde02f2e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62126e73e230cf4bd6c27cf201949c4290af84a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0399b3e212741bc5a64b8399d6266c4a150bdfe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6c1aad9b35fa083f48ce0c5926204891d82e089", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4cb9a728df66c46067b26263f5beb633aae4087", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c5d41f87f079990bf241359e3c1332d8d10fe87"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wcg4-82x5-ppxc", "CVE-2026-97411"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "067b6801-2612-3b87-b16c-b56e73fc7784", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b3e441c6ed8655a42e7b4da1b6dc7939f259d9c9 <62126e73e230cf4bd6c27cf201949c4290af84a1"}, {"id": "1531dd29-a9c6-3205-8612-3dba87c9956c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "1d86b4f5-722d-3497-93d6-bf4300700e69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "23be6b26-973b-3c4e-b2da-159461160a33", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b3e441c6ed8655a42e7b4da1b6dc7939f259d9c9 <f0399b3e212741bc5a64b8399d6266c4a150bdfe"}, {"id": "28d5d1e3-d97c-3e58-b9ea-a4affa14e396", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "66d5d000-854f-3148-8416-96d18a51032c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "6871a52b-dc71-3bd2-a5fb-efad5585152f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b3e441c6ed8655a42e7b4da1b6dc7939f259d9c9 <34c4cae51718d6f393415e01c61314c1bde02f2e"}, {"id": "84598b1e-4885-3ae5-8a7e-a0ec1d729dda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b3e441c6ed8655a42e7b4da1b6dc7939f259d9c9 <f6c1aad9b35fa083f48ce0c5926204891d82e089"}, {"id": "8934c103-009d-3541-8280-427ab2c4934f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "97e0a3ce-3544-3a4e-bb3b-9d1b7e1f9464", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "aab30dea-57f6-371b-8542-71bc2514d084", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b3e441c6ed8655a42e7b4da1b6dc7939f259d9c9 <9c1c814a662d9c81959eba591bb52b24639390f2"}, {"id": "c032de7c-c182-3484-969f-bf40bede6184", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b3e441c6ed8655a42e7b4da1b6dc7939f259d9c9 <c4cb9a728df66c46067b26263f5beb633aae4087"}, {"id": "d27fe686-da01-350e-a625-3b1654a2f5be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e7a4264f-7774-3823-9bca-39889444d203", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "pr